Comment (.github/workflows/ci-helm.yml:116):
`ct lint` never reads the caller's `ct.yaml`. `helm/chart-testing-action` sets `CT_CONFIG_DIR` to its install dir, and ct v3.14.0 (`pkg/config/config.go` L103-110) then searches only that dir. The run has no `Using config file:` line, so `validate-maintainers: false` was ignored and both mock charts failed with "chart doesn't have maintainers". Fix: pass `--config ct.yaml` when it exists (keep `--check-version-increment=false` on the command line), e.g. `cfg=(); [ -f ct.yaml ] && cfg=(--config ct.yaml); ct lint "${cfg[@]}" --all --chart-dirs "$CHARTS_DIR" --check-version-increment=false`. Also correct the comment on L113 and the README row (L267), and add a test covering the config flag (with and without ct.yaml) like the other step tests.
